    "text": "On reading old pages\nA scanned page is a picture of words, not the words. The eye\nreads it at once; a program has to work the letters out, one\nby one, from their shapes. Where the paper was clean and the\nglass was level, it does this well.\nFaint ink, a tilted sheet or a stain make it guess. Good tools\nsay how sure they are of each word, and leave the doubtful\nones for a person to judge."
